 "pdf": "ads112s14.pdf",
 "pages": "p.3 (pins), p.5 (ROC), p.11 (timing, switching), p.22-23 (data rates), p.26 (latency), p.32-34 (reset, modes), p.35-37 (SPI frame), p.40-44 (commands), p.51 (DRDY), p.54 (data format), p.56-73 (registers)",
 "notModeled": [
  "analog input, PGA, multiplexer, reference, IDACs, burn-out sources, system monitors, global chop (stored only)",
  "GPIO0-3 on the analog pins (digital in/out, FAULT output, dedicated DRDY output on GPIO3, external CLK input): the pins are analog-only in the model; GPIOx_DAT_IN read 0",
  "command bytes are matched at the start of the frame; the datasheet interprets the LAST 16 bits before CS rise, so frames padded with leading bytes (to match a STATUS/CRC output frame) are not decoded",
  "STATUS header (STATUS_EN) and SPI CRC (SPI_CRC_EN, CRC-IN/CRC-OUT bytes) are not output; register map CRC, memory CRC, fault flags",
  "continuous-read mode (CONT_READ_EN), daisy-chain (extended frames shift SDI data back out), 3-wire SPI mode and its resynchronization",
  "STATUS_MSB write-1-to-set flags (RESETn, AVDD_UVn, REF_UVn, REG_MAP_CRC_FAULTn) are read-only in the model: RESETn stays 0 after power-on",
  "CONV_COUNT conversion counter does not increment (stays Fh); STOP bit reads 0 at once",
  "conversion time is the first-conversion latency of Table 7-6/7-7 (single-shot); continuous-mode periods tDATA = OSR / fMOD are shorter; DELAY[3:0] start delay, standby-exit and restart extra latency not added; internal 4.096 MHz oscillator assumed",
  "writes to DEVICE_CFG..DIGITAL_CFG restart ongoing conversions (datasheet); not modeled",
  "SDO/DRDY: the datasheet holds it Hi-Z while CS is high and mirrors DRDY only while CS is low before the first SCLK (SDO_MODE = 1); with SDO_MODE = 0 it holds the last bit (modeled idle 0)",
  "DRDY returns high at the 8th SCLK of the MSB byte (modeled: on result read); 2 tMOD high pulse when data are not read",
  "td(RST) 500 us and td(POR) 5 ms communication delays; reading an invalid address (none with 4 address bits)",
  "unipolar straight-binary coding (CODING = 1): the 0 V code stays 0000h (it is also 0000h for twos complement)"
 ],
